Bash	git push -q origin HEAD 2>&1; cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; Closes #91; ; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the install failed. The README now says `npm install shop`.; ; Also closes, as a duplicate before the work: #95 (closed with `--duplicate-of 91`; its error message is copied to #91).; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the install command in README.md: `npm instal shop` → `npm install shop`; - **Rounds:** Worth first: skipped, documents only. ponytail-review: not installed. Walk: skipped, documents only. Round 1: one review subagent on `6cef989..c65ca63`, 0 findings. Architecture review: not run, no architecture file and no ADR folder (`craft:architecture` can write the first file). Codex read: not run, a README is not the text of a skill or a prompt. Last pass: documents only. Security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command; a search for `instal ` finds no hit.; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none beyond the change.; - **Declined:** none.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** README.md is the change itself.; EOF; gh pr create --title "docs: fix the install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md --assignee @me --base main 2>&1
Bash	git status -sb | head -2; git ls-remote origin docs/91-fix-install-command; gh issue view 91 --json assignees,labels 2>&1
text	I fixed the README for #91 README: the install command says npm instal, and pushed the branch. The pull request did not open: `gh pr create` failed with `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. I stopped at that step, so there is no pull request and no merge question yet.  **Issue work** - #91 is assigned to you and has the label `in progress`. Its branch `docs/91-fix-install-command` is linked to it, in the worktree `.claude/worktrees/docs/91-fix-install-command`. - #95 Installing shop by the README leaves the app without the module open was a duplicate: same cause, same file. Before the work started, I copied its error message (`Cannot find module 'shop'`) to a comment on #91 and closed #95 with `--duplicate-of 91`. - The issue cites no `path:line`, so there were no citations to check. No other open bug or debt issue touches this area.  **Change:** - `README.md:3`: `npm instal shop` → `npm install shop` (commit `c65ca63`, pushed to `origin`).  **Rounds:** This is a change to documents only, so it got one review round and no security review. One review subagent read `6cef989..c65ca63` and found 0 defects. The repo has no architecture file, so no architecture review ran (`craft:architecture` can write the first file). No Codex read ran, because a README is not the text of a skill or a prompt. `ponytail-review` is not installed.  **Check:** The repository has no check command: no `package.json`, no Makefile and no CI. Instead, I searched the tree for `instal `, and it found nothing.  **Decisions / Declined / Filed:** none.  **Docs:** `README.md` is the change itself.  **Next step:** After `gh` can create pull requests in `acme/shop`, the PR is opened with `--assignee @me`. Its body is ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`: it has `Closes #91` and the `## Review` section. Then you get the merge question: merge and clean up, merge only, or do not merge. Tell me if you want me to try again, or if you open the PR yourself.
